{
  "metadata": {
    "note": "Verbatim DDInter 2.0 slice for issue #167 - the two residual-bucket arms and the case that bounds the exclusion. Rows are field-for-field their KB rows in KB order, and the interaction rows are every KB pair among these drugs. Acetylsalicylic acid and Epinephrine share A01AD 'Other agents for local oral treatment' and NOTHING else, which is the duplicate-therapy claim measured live on Agnes Adams; Potassium Iodide and Acetylcysteine share S01XA 'Other ophthalmologicals' and V03AB 'Antidotes' and nothing else, which is the cross-reactivity claim. Loratadine and Desloratadine are the boundary: R06AX is residual too, but its parent R06A is 'ANTIHISTAMINES FOR SYSTEMIC USE', so both members really are antihistamines and the claim must survive. The Acetylsalicylic acid x Epinephrine and Loratadine x Desloratadine rows are rated Unknown with no mechanism, so they carry no mechanism text and cannot clear the severity floor - every chip these drugs raise here comes from the class arm alone."
  },
